;; One mutation per invariant. `:find` must occur EXACTLY ONCE in `:file` —
;; `tools/mutate.cljs` refuses otherwise, because a mutation that landed in a
;; comment or a second call site produces a red suite that proves nothing.
;;
;; ## SCOPE
;;
;; Covers the 2026-08-18 `.clj` → `.cljc` conversion of `isic.coordinator`:
;; that the R0 sentinel is the sentinel, that `noop` really is identity, that
;; the mode is read under BOTH the string and the keyword key, and that the
;; default mode is 0. It does NOT cover the taxonomy this cell will one day
;; resolve against — there is none yet — so a clean run of this table means
;; "the scaffold's routing is measured" and NOT "this cell is measured".
;;
;; ⚠ These mutations run `clojure -M:test`. The `:cljs` half is exercised by
;; `test/run_portable.cljs`, which this harness does not drive. For THIS
;; namespace the two halves are the same bytes — there is not one reader
;; conditional in it — so a mutation cannot redden one and not the other.
;; That is a property of this file, not a general one; do not carry the
;; assumption to a namespace that does branch.
;;
;; ## MEASURED 2026-08-18: 5 mutations, 4 killed, 1 SURVIVED.
;;
;; `:mode-1-routes-to-summarize-and-not-lookup` survives and is left in the
;; table. It is not a test gap that anyone can close today: `lookup` and
;; `summarize` both answer the same `NOT-FOUND-R0` sentinel at R0, so from
;; outside this cell the two modes are indistinguishable, and a test that
;; told them apart would be measuring the implementation rather than the
;; contract. Deleting the mutation would hide that. It becomes killable the
;; moment either mode returns an answer of its own.
[{:id :lookup-answers-the-r0-sentinel
  :invariant "lookup reports NOT-FOUND-R0 until taxonomy ingest lands"
  :file "src/isic/coordinator.cljc"
  :find "  (assoc state \"result\" \"NOT-FOUND-R0\"))\n\n(defn summarize"
  :replace "  (assoc state \"result\" \"FOUND\"))\n\n(defn summarize"}

 {:id :noop-does-not-stamp-the-state
  :invariant "an unrecognised mode returns the state UNCHANGED"
  :file "src/isic/coordinator.cljc"
  :find "  [state]\n  state)"
  :replace "  [state]\n  (assoc state \"result\" \"NOT-FOUND-R0\"))"}

 {:id :the-keyword-mode-key-is-read
  :invariant "`:mode` and \"mode\" are both honoured; EDN callers are not
              silently demoted to mode 0"
  :file "src/isic/coordinator.cljc"
  :find "(get state \"mode\" (get state :mode 0))"
  :replace "(get state \"mode\" 0)"}

 {:id :the-default-mode-is-lookup
  :invariant "state naming no mode at all routes to 0/lookup"
  :file "src/isic/coordinator.cljc"
  :find "(get state :mode 0))"
  :replace "(get state :mode 99))"}

 ;; Written before the tests, and expected by nobody to be interesting:
 ;; recorded because it turned out to be. See the note in the test file.
 {:id :mode-1-routes-to-summarize-and-not-lookup
  :invariant "mode 1 is a DIFFERENT mode from mode 0"
  :file "src/isic/coordinator.cljc"
  :find "    1 (summarize state)"
  :replace "    1 (lookup state)"}]
